@crew tomas
// Writer-commons, batch 1 (for the Voices sampler). Tomas's card is the head writer's. Nothing here goes past what
// STORY_ARCS.tomas has told (beats 1-4): no exam, no transfer list.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. You're new too, aren't you? I'm Tomas. Watch. I'm sort of new as well.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning! The washroom's free. Hot water till ten, then it's character-building.
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- You're up too? I keep looking at the star map instead of sleeping.
? tier>=colleague
- {hi}. I took the long way round Deck 2 again. On purpose. Mostly on purpose.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- There you are! I saved you the window seat. Well, I sat in it. Same thing.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good day! Holt nodded at me. Just once. I think it was a nod.   #funny
? mood:low
- Bit quiet today. Sort of grey inside. It usually lifts by dinner.

== near
? act:gym
- Vance said "one more kilometre" and walked off. So I'm still going. I think he's gone.   #funny
? act:work
- On patrol. The Watch office has the best view of the lift. So, of everyone, really.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I write to my little brother every week. I make the job sound exciting. It is, mostly.
? tier>=colleague
- Where I grew up, the sky was the same grey every day. Out here it's never the same twice.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night! I've named three stars. Not officially. They don't know yet.   #funny

== week1
// The arrival evening, step A12 (plans/pillar4-plan.md Part 1): after dinner Tomas finds you in the junior common
// room or Bunk 1 and you have your first chat card. Day 0 only: Sunday, before the week1.d2 flag (Tuesday 06:00).
// The head writer and the onboarding engineer may want a sharper hook (an intro-step condition).
? week1:true weekday:sun time:evening !flag:week1.d2
- Oh good, you found the common room. It took me three days. I'm Tomas, from the bunk.
- How was dinner? Did Brennan call you "love"? She calls everyone that. You get used to it.
- That's how you chat, by the way. Tap someone and talk. I was terrible at it at first.
- Ask me anything. I know everything. Well. A week's worth of everything.   #funny
- Sleep whenever you like. Lights out is ten, Chloe says. Chloe means it.
- I'm really glad you're here. I was the newest for a whole week. It was a long week.   #warm
- Night, {me}. If you wake up and don't know where you are, that's normal. It's Deck 4.   #funny

// Writer-commons, batch 4: up to about 60. Exam lines only from beat:tomas.5; the transfer list from beat:tomas.6.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}! Did you see the stars on the way past? Proper ones tonight.
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {hi}. I went the long way round Deck 2 again. I found a new long way.   #funny
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- There you are! I thought the lift had eaten you. It does that. I think.   #funny
? tier>=colleague deck:4
- {hi}, {me}. Bunk's tidy. Well, my half is. Yours is... characterful.   #funny
? tier>=close
- {hi}, {nick}. I saved you the last biscuit. You've no idea how hard that was.   #warm

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- See you back at the bunk. Don't get lost. Says me.
- Right. Patrol. Wish me luck. I mean, it's a corridor. Wish me luck anyway.   #funny
? tier>=colleague time:night
- Night, {me}. If you see a shooting star, it's mine. I asked first.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Thanks for this. Really. You always make me feel less lost.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- All right, I think. Sort of medium. Medium's fine, isn't it?
? mood:low tier>=friend
- Bit homesick. It comes and goes. It's going, now you're here.   #warm

== near
? act:leisure
- The window seat's free! Quick. Before someone else notices it.
? act:meal
- Is this the stew? I think it's the stew. It's probably the stew.   #funny
? deck:2
- Deck 2 always feels like a museum. A nice one. You whisper without meaning to.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Vance talked me onto the treadmill. I don't know how. I was walking past.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I'm not sure I've found my place yet. I'm looking. That counts, doesn't it?
? beat:tomas.5 tier>=friend
- Still haven't told Holt about the exam. Don't remind me. Do remind me. Soon.

== invite
? trad:observatory-night tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night tonight! Come up? I'll show you the stars I've named.
? trad:film tier>=acquaintance
- Film night! I'll save you a seat. Not the one by the speaker. Trust me.
? trad:running tier>=colleague
- Running club? Vance will be there. Come and stand between us.   #funny

== accept
- {yes}! I'll be there. I'll probably be early. I'm always early. It's a nerves thing.
- Yes! Thanks for asking. Nobody asks me things. Well, you do.   #warm

== decline
- I can't, sorry. Patrol. But ask me again? I'd really like you to ask me again.
- Not tonight. I promised my brother a long letter. Another time?

== missed
- I waited for you. That's all right. Something came up, I expect. Next time?
- You didn't come. Did I get the time wrong? I usually get the time wrong.

== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday! I wasn't going to say. I've said. Is there cake? Is that rude?   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I made you a card. It's got a star on it. Well, a dot. A star-ish dot.   #warm

== hint
- Got a minute? Not a big thing. A medium thing.

== week1
? week1:true weekday:mon time:morning
- Morning! Washroom, then breakfast. Breakfast's till eight. Left at the end. Probably.
? week1:true weekday:thu
- Inspection today. I've folded everything. I've folded my socks. Is that normal?   #funny
? week1:true weekday:fri tier>=acquaintance
- Sowing morning's tomorrow! You plant your own seedling. Come with me? Film night after.
? week1:true weekday:sat time:morning
- Ready? Garden. Seedling. Bring your hands. That's all you need. And maybe a towel.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance act:work
- {hi}! I'm on patrol. Very official. Watch out. I'm watching. That's the job.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning weekday:mon
- Monday! Fresh start. I've got a list. I've lost the list. Fresh start.   #funny

== near
? deck:3
- The promenade at this hour! You can see half the ship from here. Well, a corridor.
? act:off
- Rest day. I'm going to write to my brother and then look at the stars. Big plans.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Back home the sky was grey every day. Here I've got a whole star map. Under my bunk.
? tier>=colleague
- Holt terrifies me. In a good way. I think. Is there a good way? There must be.   #funny

== feel
? mood:high tier>=colleague
- Good day! I found the laundry on the first try. That's a first. I'm a new man.   #funny

== about
? bond:best
- {best}'s the best. They always know where they're going. I just follow.   #warm
? aff:vance:friend
- Vance runs next to me on the treadmill now. Doesn't talk. Very encouraging. I think.   #funny

// Writer 3, batch 1: callbacks (told: is said once; mem: is a fond memory that can come back), visits at your bunk
// (friend tier and up; he lives there, so he knocks anyway), and notes left on your bunk (the game adds his name).
// Moment memories are moment.tomas.<word> from beats 5-7; heard.<key> is what a friend told him.

== callback
? told:moment.tomas.promised
- You never told anyone. About the exam. I knew you wouldn't. I still checked. Sorry.   #warm
? told:moment.tomas.passed
- "That's the one that counts." I wrote it inside my locker. Small. Holt won't see.   #warm
? told:moment.tomas.blanket
- The blanket held! Holt stared at it for ages, then walked on. That's a pass. I think.   #funny
? told:moment.tomas.listened
- Thanks for listening. About the list. I only read it twice a day now. Progress.   #warm
? told:moment.tomas.showed
- I did show you round, didn't I? I keep thinking about that. I got one thing right.   #warm
? told:moment.tomas.observatory !beat:tomas.7
- Observatory night's coming. The star map's rolled up and ready. Is that keen? It's keen.   #funny
? told:moment.tomas.shown
- Just left of the bright one. My left. You remembered! You did, didn't you?   #funny
? mem:moment.tomas.staying
- Still here. Still staying. I check every morning. Still true.   #warm
? told:moment.tomas.home
- Holt's put me down to meet the next shuttle. Me! I've been practising "This way."   #funny
? told:came.observatory-night
- You came up! Did you see the one I named? The wobbly one. That's mine.   #funny
? told:came.film
- Thanks for coming to film night. I cried at the bit with the boat. Don't tell anyone.   #funny
? told:came.running
- You came running! Vance said "adequate" about you. He said "noted" about me.   #funny
? told:fav.fetch
- Thanks for fetching that. I'd have gone the long way. You know I would.   #warm
? told:fav.lamp
- My lamp works! I can read my brother's letters at night now. Thanks, really.   #warm
? told:fav.job
- You did my job for me. I owe you. I've written it down. I'll lose the paper.   #funny
? told:gift.star
- I put your present by the star map. Two skies under one bunk now. Thank you.   #warm
? told:gift.card
- I kept your card. It's in with my brother's letters. That's the good pile.   #warm
? told:gift.sweet
- Those sweets lasted two days. I rationed. Well, I tried. One and a half days.   #funny
? told:fixed.lift
- Was it you who fixed the lift? It sounds happier. I can hear it from the Watch office.
? told:bday
- You came to find me on my birthday. My brother always does that. Now two people do.   #warm
? told:heard.moment.rina
- Rina says you're all right. From Rina that's practically a medal.   #funny
? told:heard.moment.pell
- Pell says you're the best. He says that about anyone with biscuits. But he meant it.   #funny

== visit
- Knock, knock. I know I live here. It felt polite.   #funny
- Are you busy? I'm not. I've been not busy all evening. It's lonely, not being busy.   #funny
- Can I sit? I wrote my brother a whole page about you. Nice things. Mostly.   #warm
- I found biscuits. Brennan's. Don't ask where. Want one? Want two?
? time:night
- Can't sleep. I've been counting the stars on my map. Forty-one. Night, then.

== note
- Came to find you. You were out. You're always out! Saving the ship, probably. See you at the bunk.
- Left you a biscuit under your pillow. Don't sit on it. If you've sat on it, sorry.   #funny
- Went the long way round Deck 2 again. Found a new window. I'll show you tomorrow.
- Your blanket was falling off, so I folded it. Badly. Holt would weep.   #funny
? trad:observatory-night
- Observatory's open tonight. Come up if you see this in time. If not, I'll tell you all about it.

// Writer 3, batch 3: towards 120. Seasons, places, bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters), cues. Rest days
// Fri, Sat (the game's roster); rest-day lines use act:off. Why he left home only at close.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance place:mess
- {hi}! Sit here. I saved a seat. Well, I put my tray on it.
? tier>=friend time:morning
- Morning, {nick}. I dreamt I was lost on Deck 2. Woke up on Deck 4. Progress.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance season:lanterns
- The lanterns are up! Everything looks like a story. A nice one.
? tier>=acquaintance season:sowing
- Sowing! How's your seedling? Mine's leaning. Towards the light, I hope.
? tier>=acquaintance season:greening
- It's all green in the garden. I keep going in just to breathe.
? tier>=acquaintance season:harvest
- Harvest! Brennan says I can help carry. I've been practising carrying.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Off on patrol. If you see Holt, tell him I'm already there. Early. Obviously.   #funny
? tier>=close
- See you later, {nick}. Back at the bunk. Mind the star map.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high tier>=friend
- Brilliant day. My brother wrote. Two pages. About the weather. It was grey.   #funny
? mood:low tier>=colleague
- Quiet day. I'm writing to my brother. Saying things on paper helps.

== near
? place:observatory
- Every time I come up here, there's more. I don't know how. There just is.
? act:breakfast
- Toast. Always toast. My brother says I'm boring. I say toast is reliable.   #funny
? act:dinner
- {dish}? Is that what it is? I'll say yes and eat it.   #funny
? place:lounge
- The bow windows! You can see where we're going. Well, where we're pointing.
? act:wash
- Hot water's still on! Quick, before it's character-building.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- On the farm moon there was one road and three fences. Here there are hundreds of doors.
? tier>=colleague
- My brother wants to be a pilot now. Last month a cook. I'm keeping up.   #funny
? tier>=close
- I was scared I'd stay home for the rest of my life. So I signed up. Scared's useful.

== joy
? tier>=colleague
- The Wren's passed more stars than I'll ever count. I'm trying to catch up.
? tier>=friend
- Best bit of my week? Observatory night. Second best? Film night with the bunk.   #warm

== invite
? tier>=colleague time:evening
- Observatory after dinner? I've found a new star. Possibly a smudge.   #funny
? trad:quiz tier>=acquaintance
- Quiz tonight! I'm useless at it. Will you be useless with me?   #funny

== about
? aff:holt:friend
- Holt said "Good" to me today. One word. I've told my brother twice.   #funny
? bond:mentor
- {mentor} looks out for me. Like I look out for you. It goes down the line.   #warm

== smalltalk
- Is it left here? It's left. It's probably left.   #funny
- Look at the stars out there. Every single time.
- The long way's nicer. Honestly.
- I've folded my blanket three times. It's fine.   #funny
? act:work
- Patrol. All quiet. Very quiet. Too quiet? No. Fine.   #funny

== rumour
- Heard something on patrol. Is it gossip if it's Watch?
- I wasn't listening. I've just got very good ears.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- The storm's here. Holt says stay calm. I'm staying calm. Very calm. Loudly.   #funny
? cue:event.ionStorm.afterglow
- Did you see the sky after the storm? All those colours. I wrote my brother three pages.
? cue:harvest
- Harvest! The garden smells like home. A nicer home. With more plants.
? cue:repair.lift.you
- Was that you on the lift? I rode it twice to check. For the Watch.   #funny

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- Holt said your name today. In a normal voice. That's very good, from Holt.   #funny
? rep:theirs
- The whole Watch office knows you now. You're on our side of the lift.   #warm
? you:kind
- People keep saying you're kind. I knew first. I'm just saying. I knew first.   #funny
? you:chatty
- Everyone says you talk to everyone. Good. Someone has to. I get nervous.   #funny

// Writer 3, batch 8: thanks for a gift (gift: loved | liked | polite, or the gift's tag; dialogue 0.43.10).

== gift
? gift:star
- Oh, wow. For me? This is going right by the star map. Right by it. Thank you, really.   #warm
? gift:loved
- Oh, wow. This is perfect. How did you know? Did someone tell you? Nobody knew.   #warm
? gift:liked
- For me? Thanks, really. I'll put it somewhere I can see it. Somewhere safe-ish.
? gift:polite
- Oh! Thank you. I don't know what it is. I'll find out. That's half the fun, isn't it?   #funny
